#: src/reference/symbol-editor.md:134
msgid ""
"Action coordinates are **millimetres**, unlike JSON document coordinates. "
"Placement snaps the insertion point to the destination page grid; it never "
"moves a pin within the symbol. A different symbol/page grid is refused "
"before changing the project, and the refusal offers a new page with the "
"symbol's grid: **Place on a new page with its grid** (`symbol.new_page`) "
"places the published symbol there and selects it while the draft is saved to "
"a library and unchanged since, and **Test on a new page** places a test copy "
"otherwise. Replacing or opening over a dirty draft requires `discard: true`; "
"`symbol.close` keeps the draft unless it has `discard: true`, and "
"`symbol.new` without a key or name returns to it, or with `discard: true` "
"starts a fresh draft. `app.quit` with `discard: true` discards an unsaved "
"draft. `ui.describe` and the script state expose the open editor and "
"validation findings. [The tutorial](../tutorials/symbol-editor.md) includes "
"a complete six-pin example."
