#: src/reference/symbol-editor.md:174
msgid ""
"A new drawing starts with a generic black-box function. In **Electrical "
"data**, under **Function definition**, choose its function type and set each "
"pin's potential role and flags, or assign an existing library function. "
"Existing assigned functions remain read-only. Internal connections and less "
"common fields are available through **Advanced document**. Typing `FE` as a "
"designation changes the printed label; select the FE potential role to give "
"it electrical meaning. Text slots obtain tags, technical data and function "
"text from the placed device; the editor shows sample values. Library "
"publication does not update already placed copies. The EPLAN importer does "
"not create complete manufacturer part records, and SLK connection "
"designations are provisional numbers until the function is reviewed."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/symbol-editor.md:182
msgid ""
"Keep `custom.slk` beside the complete `custom.sdb` folder (or the sibling "
"folder named in the descriptor). Only the Symbol, Variant, Instance and Blob "
"drawing tables are read. No EPLAN installation, script, workstation record "
"or lock file is used. The supported subset is based on an inspected public "
"library sample; it is not a vendor-certified database reader. Unsupported "
"versions and legacy descriptor encodings are refused. Other primitives, "
"static text, fills and custom line styles are reported as incomplete. Only A "
"is reconstructed; EW then derives B–H, which can differ from separately "
"authored EPLAN variants. Review geometry, every connection, function "
"semantics and licence before publishing. Missing connection records are "
"reported, never invented. Companion tables are limited to 4 MiB each and "
"reconstructed streams to 64 MiB total; oversized libraries are refused."
msgstr ""

