#: src/explanation/index.md:25
msgid "For users of other programs"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/index.md:27
msgid ""
"[EPLAN and EW](eplan-and-ew.md): the EPLAN concepts, such as functions, "
"device tags, CDPs and message management, and what they are called and how "
"they differ in EW."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/index.md:29
msgid ""
"[QElectroTech and EW](qet-and-ew.md): the QElectroTech concepts, such as "
"elements, master and slave, folio reports and conductors, and their EW "
"counterparts."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:3
msgid ""
"If you come from EPLAN Electric P8, most of EW will feel familiar: a project "
"of pages, devices with functions, parts from a database, potentials and "
"reports that update themselves. The words are mostly the same too. This page "
"takes each EPLAN concept in turn: the EW term, what is the same, what "
"differs, and where to find it in EW's window. The "
"[glossary](../reference/glossary.md) lists every term in one table, and each "
"EPLAN term below is also an alias in the command palette."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:9
msgid "Function"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:11 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:12
msgid "**EW term:** [Function](../reference/glossary.md#function)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:13
msgid ""
"**The same:** a function is one symbol's worth of a device: a coil, a "
"contact, a pin group, placed on a page. **What differs:** a function always "
"belongs to a device in EW; there is no function without a device tag, and "
"placing a symbol creates its device at once. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ "
"Place ▸ Symbol…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:17
msgid "Device, Device tag, DT, BMK"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:19 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:20
msgid "**EW term:** [Device](../reference/glossary.md#device)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:21
msgid ""
"**The same:** a device is the physical object with its device tag (DT, the "
"German BMK), made of functions that may sit on several pages. **What "
"differs:** EW derives the tag from the project's numbering scheme and the "
"structure, so a tag is never typed text: renumbering changes every page, "
"report and label at once, and a tag you want to keep is frozen. **In the "
"window:** **Draw ▸ Place ▸ Device from part…** and **Draw ▸ Arrange ▸ "
"Renumber devices…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:26
msgid "Part, Article"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:28 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:28
msgid "**EW term:** [Part](../reference/glossary.md#part)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:30
msgid ""
"**The same:** a part is the orderable article with its manufacturer, order "
"number and technical data, assigned to a device. **What differs:** the "
"project embeds a copy of each part it uses, so it opens and prints without "
"the library; updating the copy from the library is a command you run. **In "
"the window:** **Edit ▸ Choose part…**. See [Choose "
"parts](../how-to/choose-parts.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:35
msgid "CDP, Connection definition point"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:37 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:36
msgid "**EW term:** [Wire marker](../reference/glossary.md#wire-marker)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:39
msgid ""
"**The same:** you set a wire's cross-section, colour or number at a point on "
"the wire. **What differs:** in EW the value belongs to the wire itself, and "
"the wire marker is only the label that shows it on the page; potentials and "
"profiles give the default, and a value set on the wire is an override. **In "
"the window:** **Draw ▸ Annotate ▸ Wire marker**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:46 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:44
msgid ""
"**EW term:** [Interruption "
"point](../reference/glossary.md#interruption-point)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:48
msgid ""
"**The same:** an interruption point continues a potential at another point "
"of the same name, in star or chain mode, with cross-references. **What "
"differs:** the pairing is checked: a point without a partner and a star with "
"two sources are findings in the Messages pane. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ "
"Connect ▸ Interruption point**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:52
msgid "Basic project"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:54 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:52
msgid "**EW term:** [Basic project](../reference/glossary.md#basic-project)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:56
msgid ""
"**The same:** a new project starts from a basic project that holds the "
"company's frames, settings and structure. **What differs:** EW ships one "
"basic project and the company standard wizard makes your own from it. **In "
"the window:** **File ▸ New project…** and **Project ▸ Company standard "
"wizard…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:60
msgid "Form, Plot frame"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:62 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:59
msgid ""
"**EW term:** [Frame and title "
"block](../reference/glossary.md#frame-and-title-block)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:64
msgid ""
"**The same:** the frame and title block print around every page, filled from "
"the project's and the page's data. **What differs:** report pages and "
"drawing pages take their frame from the project's frame settings by page "
"type, and a title-block value is bound to the project, its revision or its "
"page, not typed per page. **In the window:** **Project ▸ Company standard "
"wizard…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:69
msgid "Message management"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:71
msgid "**EW term:** [Messages](../reference/glossary.md#messages)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:73
msgid ""
"**The same:** the checks report messages that you can sort, jump to and "
"accept. **What differs:** the checks run while you draw, not only on demand, "
"and each finding names its rule, which has a page in the [rule "
"reference](../reference/rules/index.md); accepting a finding is a waiver "
"with a reason. **In the window:** **Check ▸ Messages**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:78
msgid "Main function, Auxiliary function"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:80 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:66
msgid ""
"**EW term:** [Main and auxiliary "
"function](../reference/glossary.md#main-and-auxiliary-function)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:82
msgid ""
"**The same:** a coil is the main function, its contacts are auxiliary "
"functions, and the contact image lists them with cross-references. **What "
"differs:** a contact joins its coil's device when you place it on the coil's "
"tag; the contacts the part offers are checked against the ones you draw. "
"**In the window:** **Draw ▸ Place ▸ Symbol…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:86
msgid "Connection"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:88 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:74
msgid "**EW term:** [Connection](../reference/glossary.md#connection)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:90
msgid ""
"**The same:** connections join connection points and follow the drawing. "
"**What differs:** EW builds the physical wires from the drawn connections, "
"junctions and interruption points, so the wire list follows the drawing "
"without an update step. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ Connect ▸ Wire**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:94 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:80
msgid "Terminal strip"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:96 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:82
msgid "**EW term:** [Terminal strip](../reference/glossary.md#terminal-strip)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:98
msgid ""
"**The same:** a terminal strip is a device whose terminals are functions, "
"with an editor for their order, bridges and accessories. **What differs:** "
"the strip editor is a table you edit cell by cell, and every edit is one "
"undo step. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ Place ▸ Terminal strip** and **Edit ▸ "
"Strip editor**. See [A terminal strip and a "
"cable](../tutorials/terminal-strip-and-cable.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:103
msgid ""
"Structure identifier, Identifier block, Higher-level function, Mounting "
"location"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:105 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:91
msgid "**EW term:** [Structure node](../reference/glossary.md#structure-node)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:107
msgid ""
"**The same:** the higher-level function (`=`) and the mounting location "
"(`+`) structure the project, and a device's full tag carries them. **What "
"differs:** a structure node is a record of its own, so renaming it renames "
"every tag under it; EW keeps a code as one token and never splits it again. "
"**In the window:** **Project ▸ Setup ▸ Structure node…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:114 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:99
msgid "**EW term:** [Black box](../reference/glossary.md#black-box)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:116
msgid ""
"**The same:** a black box stands for a device that has no symbol, with "
"connection points on its outline. **What differs:** nothing much; a black "
"box is a function of its device like any symbol. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ "
"Place ▸ Black box…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:122 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:106
msgid "**EW term:** [Structure box](../reference/glossary.md#structure-box)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:124
msgid ""
"**The same:** a dashed frame that assigns what it encloses to a function or "
"location. **What differs:** nothing much; the assignment shows in the tags "
"at once. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ Annotate ▸ Structure box**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:127
msgid "Report, Update reports, Embedded report"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:129 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:113
msgid "**EW term:** [Report block](../reference/glossary.md#report-block)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:131
msgid ""
"**The same:** report pages such as the terminal diagram, the cable list and "
"the parts list are generated from the project. **What differs:** there is no "
"update step: a report block is regenerated whenever the project changes, and "
"its pages are always current. **In the window:** **View ▸ Panels ▸ "
"Navigators ▸ Report blocks**. See [Reports and "
"PDF](../tutorials/reports-and-pdf.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:136
msgid "Potential, Potential definition point"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:138
msgid "**EW term:** [Potential](../reference/glossary.md#potential)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:140
msgid ""
"**The same:** a potential is a connected electrical node with a name, a type "
"and a voltage, set by a definition on one of its connections. **What "
"differs:** potentials are checked: two definitions that disagree, a "
"protective conductor with the wrong colour or a switched neutral are "
"findings. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ Connect ▸ Define potential…**. See "
"[Define a supply potential](../how-to/define-supply-potential.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:145
msgid "Cross-reference, Contact image"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:147 src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:121
msgid "**EW term:** [Cross-reference](../reference/glossary.md#cross-reference)"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/eplan-and-ew.md:149
msgid ""
"**The same:** cross-references point from a coil to its contacts and from an "
"interruption point to its partner, and the contact image under a coil lists "
"the contacts. **What differs:** a cross-reference is computed, never text, "
"so it cannot go stale; one that points outside the frame is a finding. **In "
"the window:** **Page ▸ Go ▸ Follow cross-reference**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:3
msgid ""
"If you come from QElectroTech, EW draws pages the same way, but it knows "
"more about what you draw: every symbol is a function of a device, every line "
"is a connection that carries a potential, and terminals, cables and reports "
"follow from the drawing. This page takes each QElectroTech concept in turn: "
"the EW term, what is the same, what differs, and where to find it in EW's "
"window. The [glossary](../reference/glossary.md) lists every term in one "
"table, and each QElectroTech term below is also an alias in the command "
"palette. To bring a QElectroTech project over, see [Importing a QElectroTech "
"project](../tutorials/import-qet.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:10
msgid "Element, Element instance"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:14
msgid ""
"**The same:** you pick a symbol from the collection and place it on a folio. "
"**What differs:** the placed symbol is a function of a device, not a free "
"element; the device holds the tag, the part and the other functions. **In "
"the window:** **Draw ▸ Place ▸ Symbol…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:18
msgid "Element label"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:22
msgid ""
"**The same:** a label such as -K1 names the element. **What differs:** in EW "
"the label is the device's tag, derived from the numbering scheme and the "
"structure, so you do not type it; all functions of one device share it. **In "
"the window:** **Draw ▸ Arrange ▸ Renumber devices…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:26
msgid "Manufacturer reference"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:30
msgid ""
"**The same:** the element can name the article you order. **What differs:** "
"a part is a record with its manufacturer, order number and data, embedded in "
"the project and listed in the parts list. **In the window:** **Edit ▸ Choose "
"part…**. See [Choose parts](../how-to/choose-parts.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:34
msgid "Conductor text"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:38
msgid ""
"**The same:** a text on the wire shows its number or function. **What "
"differs:** the number is a property of the wire, derived by the numbering "
"scheme; the wire marker only shows it. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ Annotate "
"▸ Wire marker**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:42
msgid "Folio report"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:46
msgid ""
"**The same:** a folio report continues a conductor on another folio, with a "
"reference to it. **What differs:** an interruption point continues a "
"potential by its name and is paired by EW; an unpaired point is a finding. "
"**In the window:** **Draw ▸ Connect ▸ Interruption point**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:50
msgid "Template project"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:54
msgid ""
"**The same:** a new project starts from a template. **What differs:** the "
"basic project also holds the company's check scheme and numbering, and the "
"company standard wizard makes your own. **In the window:** **File ▸ New "
"project…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:57
msgid "Title-block template"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:61
msgid ""
"**The same:** a template draws the title block and fills its fields. **What "
"differs:** the fields are bound to the project, the revision and the page, "
"so a value is set once. **In the window:** **Project ▸ Company standard "
"wizard…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:64
msgid "Master/slave, Master, Slave"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:68
msgid ""
"**The same:** a coil is the master and its contacts are slaves, linked with "
"cross-references. **What differs:** the contacts are functions of the coil's "
"device, and the part says how many it has; drawing more is a finding. **In "
"the window:** **Draw ▸ Place ▸ Symbol…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:72
msgid "Conductor"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:76
msgid ""
"**The same:** a conductor joins two terminals of elements. **What differs:** "
"a connection belongs to a potential and becomes part of a physical wire with "
"a cross-section, colour and number, which the wire list and the terminal "
"diagram show. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ Connect ▸ Wire**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:84
msgid ""
"**The same:** terminals are grouped in strips with a terminal-strip editor. "
"**What differs:** a terminal strip is a device, its terminals are its "
"functions, and the terminal diagram is generated from it. **In the window:** "
"**Draw ▸ Place ▸ Terminal strip** and **Edit ▸ Strip editor**. See [A "
"terminal strip and a cable](../tutorials/terminal-strip-and-cable.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:89
msgid "Plant, Location"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:93
msgid ""
"**The same:** plant and location codes group the elements and print in their "
"labels. **What differs:** a structure node is a record, and a device's tag "
"carries it, so renaming the node renames every tag below it. **In the "
"window:** **Project ▸ Setup ▸ Structure node…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:97
msgid "Rectangle"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:101
msgid ""
"**The same:** a rectangle stands for a device that has no symbol of its own. "
"**What differs:** a black box has connection points on its outline, so wires "
"connect to it. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ Place ▸ Black box…**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:104
msgid "Dotted shape"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:108
msgid ""
"**The same:** a dotted frame groups what it encloses. **What differs:** a "
"structure box assigns its contents to a function or location, which their "
"tags then carry. **In the window:** **Draw ▸ Annotate ▸ Structure box**."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:111
msgid "Summary, Nomenclature, Folio list"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:115
msgid ""
"**The same:** the folio list and the nomenclature are generated pages. "
"**What differs:** a report block is always current, and EW offers more of "
"them: terminal diagrams, cable lists and the parts list. **In the window:** "
"**View ▸ Panels ▸ Navigators ▸ Report blocks**. See [Reports and "
"PDF](../tutorials/reports-and-pdf.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:119
msgid "Cross-reference"
msgstr ""

#: src/explanation/qet-and-ew.md:123
msgid ""
"**The same:** a reference points from a coil to its contacts and from a "
"folio report to its partner. **What differs:** EW computes it from the "
"model, so it cannot go stale. **In the window:** **Page ▸ Go ▸ Follow "
"cross-reference**."
msgstr ""

